From 8fe423c72af622369de56d08fa5300c9221edcef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fermata Dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:20:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add Settings option to enable/disable Internet access

Adds an ENABLE_INTERNET preference (default on). When disabled:
- App.isInternetAccessBlocked() short-circuits the in-house HTTP stack
  (HttpConnection.connect fails fast with an IOException) and
- FermataWebClient.shouldInterceptRequest serves a local 'Internet disabled'
  page for main-frame WebView/YouTube navigation,
with a one-time toast notifying the user. Exposed via a Settings toggle.

Files:
- depends/utils/.../app/App.java: isInternetAccessBlocked()/onInternetBlocked() hooks
- depends/utils/.../net/http/HttpConnection.java: block check in connect()
- fermata/.../FermataApplication.java: pref-backed override + toast
- fermata/.../ui/activity/MainActivityPrefs.java: ENABLE_INTERNET pref (default true)
- fermata/.../ui/fragment/SettingsFragment.java: Settings toggle row
- fermata/.../res/values/strings.xml: internet_access strings
- modules/web/.../FermataWebClient.java: WebView main-frame intercept

Verified: auto-variant compile (compileAutoDebugSources) BUILD SUCCESSFUL.
