From e1a8e8ba14b94ff0d5f58d66fc1c0442cd32a702 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fermata Dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:43:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Remove Favorites from the default bottom navigation

Drops 'favorites' from the default nav-bar layout in
NavBarMediator.getLayout(). The Favorites feature is unchanged and still
reachable via:
- the item context menu ('Add to favorites' / MediaItemMenuHandler),
- voice commands (VoiceCommandHandler -> showFragment(favorites_fragment)),
- the media-library Favorites root and the playback-notification favorite button.

The getItems() 'favorites' case is kept so a user who already has Favorites
in their saved NAV_BAR_ITEMS_* layout still sees it (no pref wipe); it is
simply no longer a default tab.

